WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.940
A randomized trial finds five-year colonoscopy intervals after polypermoval match three-year results for colorectal cancer prevention. This is Planetterrian Daily, episode 186. A randomized trial directly compared surveillance colonoscopy performed at three years versus five years after initial polypermoval. The five-year interval met the criteria for non-inferiority on the primary outcome of colorectal cancer incidents measured across five years of follow.

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:35.340
up. Participants assigned to more frequent examinations had additional lesions identified

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:40.980
during the extra procedures. Those extra detections did not translate into a meaningful reduction

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:47.340
in colorectal cancer diagnoses over the study period. The findings were published in NEJM.

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:54.200
Next up, researchers constructed the first functional DNA computer using molecular components that

00:00:54.200 --> 00:01:00.200
operate as logic gates. DNA strands were engineered to carry out computational steps through

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:06.140
specific binding and release reactions. The system completed defined calculations without relying

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:11.980
on electronic hardware. Full technical details of the molecular architecture appear in the current

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:20.000
nature publication. Teams at MIT's CSAIL, along with collaborating institutions, train neural networks

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:23.860
works on individual patient medical imaging data collected before surgery.

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:29.500
The resulting models generated personalized predictions that guided intraoperative decisions.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:34.500
Integration of the networks into surgical workflows aimed to reduce complications.

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:39.200
Accuracy during procedures formed a second target of that integration effort.

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:41.940
The complete study is reported in nature.

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:45.900
Preoperative scans supplied the data used to train each network.

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:51.520
work. A new computational framework converts static research papers into interactive agents

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:57.640
capable of answering questions and exchanging information with other agents. Each agent retains

00:01:57.640 --> 00:02:03.380
the content and logic of its source paper while enabling cross-paper queries. The method

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:09.080
was developed to change how scientific knowledge is accessed and synthesized. Implementation details

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:14.740
are provided in the latest nature issue. Two years of daily multivitamin supplementation

00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:20.100
produced measurable shifts in seven distinct metabolomic aging clocks toward younger values.

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:26.860
The observed change corresponded to approximately 0.5 to one year of reduced metabolic aging,

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:33.380
relative to placebo. Participants also showed lower metabolic risk scores associated with major

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:40.300
cardiovascular events, kidney disease, dementia, asthma, cataracts, glaucoma, liver disease,

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:46.120
skin cancer and prostate cancer. Prior Cosmos publications had already reported

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:50.300
modest cognitive improvements and slower epigenetic aging with the same

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:55.000
intervention. The newest clock and risk score results lost statistical

00:02:55.000 --> 00:03:00.200
significance after correction for multiple comparisons. Investigators developed an

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:04.460
analytical approach that derives an estimate of biological aging rate from a

00:03:04.460 --> 00:03:09.160
single biological sample. The method bypasses the need for repeated measurements

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:14.860
over time. Potential applications include faster evaluation of interventions intended to

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:22.060
modify aging trajectories. Government records now confirm that Japan has 100,000 residents aged 100

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:28.220
years or older. The milestone results from decades of incremental gains in life expectancy across the

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:35.140
population. Earlier thresholds such as the first recorded centenarian once generated widespread media

00:03:35.140 --> 00:03:40.160
attention that has since become routine. Certain bird species have been observed using

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:45.480
geothermal sites in a manner similar to natural saunas. These locations serve thermal

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:50.580
regulatory functions that resemble those of health spas. Visits to the sites may assist

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:56.360
birds with maintaining feather condition. Control of external parasites is another possible benefit

00:03:56.360 --> 00:04:01.920
from the elevated ambient temperatures. The observations come from reports in Fizz.org.

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:06.160
Geothermal areas provide the necessary heat for these purposes.

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:12.440
Stanford investigators generated xenocortical mice in which up to 92% of cortical tissue

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:13.860
consists of human cells.

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:19.840
Multiple synchronized cameras recorded the animal's position and velocity while they explored

00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:20.900
controlled arenas.

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:26.080
The resulting behavioral data allowed direct comparison of human-derived neural circuits

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:28.540
with typical mouse cortex function.

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:34.140
The model provides a platform for examining human specific aspects of brain development

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:34.920
and disease.

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:40.700
A population study identified a measurable longevity advantage among individuals whose

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:42.420
parents reached age 100.

00:04:42.820 --> 00:04:47.880
The benefit persisted after statistical adjustment for some shared environmental and lifestyle

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:48.620
variables.

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:54.880
The finding adds to evidence that familial factors influence lifespan beyond obvious behavioral

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:55.480
inheritance.

00:04:55.480 --> 00:05:01.820
U.C. Riverside Analysis of Urban Fire Patterns showed that higher income neighborhoods located

00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:06.640
on hillsides and in canyons experienced 30% greater fire incidents.

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:12.600
These same areas demonstrate faster recovery times after fire damage compared with lower

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:17.420
income zones, likely due to differences in resources and rebuilding capacity.

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:23.620
University of Canterbury researchers surveyed participants in regular tabletop role-playing

00:05:23.620 --> 00:05:29.100
sessions. Regular involvement correlated with stronger reported social connections and

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:34.080
an increased sense of belonging. These social outcomes were linked to measurable support

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:40.120
for mental health indicators in the study groups. A new assessment of Atlantic menhaden populations

00:05:40.120 --> 00:05:45.800
determined that natural mortality rates had been substantially overestimated in earlier models.

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:50.840
The corrected figures indicate the stock may support lower levels of fishing pressure

00:05:50.840 --> 00:05:52.500
than previously calculated.

00:05:53.140 --> 00:05:55.440
The species serves as a critical forage base

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:58.200
for multiple predators along the US East coast.

00:05:59.020 --> 00:06:02.220
Laboratory analysis identified distinct lipid profiles

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:04.800
in black and green Japanese rice varieties

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:07.460
that differ from those in standard white rice.

00:06:08.060 --> 00:06:11.060
These varieties also exhibited slower digestion rates

00:06:11.060 --> 00:06:12.240
in model systems.

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:16.080
The combination of lipid composition and digestion kinetics

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:19.220
may contribute to more stable post-meal blood glucose

00:06:19.220 --> 00:06:27.280
responses. The compound targets the PRX3 antioxidant pathway that mesothelioma cells rely on to manage

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:34.300
oxidative stress. In an early phase clinical trial, the agent achieved disease control in 67% of

00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:40.660
enrolled patients. Survival outcomes in the initial cohort were described as encouraging relative to

00:06:40.660 --> 00:06:46.940
historical expectations for this cancer type. Most people assume the kidneys only become active when fluid

00:06:46.940 --> 00:06:50.200
intake increases or when waste builds up noticeably.

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:55.840
In reality, the kidneys maintain continuous filtration regardless of immediate fluid status.

00:06:56.440 --> 00:07:01.920
Right now, as you listen, roughly 1 million nephrons in each kidney are forcing plasma

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:07.920
through specialized capillaries, while reclaiming water, ions, and nutrients before the filtrate

00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:08.760
reaches the bladder.

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:14.020
The entire blood volume passes through this system approximately every 30 minutes under

00:07:14.020 --> 00:07:14.980
resting conditions.

00:07:14.980 --> 00:07:21.660
That produces a memorable number, about 180 liters of filtrate are generated daily, yet

00:07:21.660 --> 00:07:25.960
only 1-2 liters of urine are excreted after extensive reabsorption.

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:31.820
The constant workload explains why even modest reductions in blood flow can alter electrolyte

00:07:31.820 --> 00:07:32.580
balance quickly.

